# .chezmoiignore
#
# Negation patterns always take priority over includes (chezmoi semantics).
# MAINTENANCE: When adding a new managed file under a broadly-ignored directory (.config/, .gemini/, .ssh/, Library/), add a matching negation here.
# Stale negations surface as a non-empty 'chezmoi unmanaged' — that output must always be empty.
# NOTE: '/**' patterns match the directory itself too (doublestar semantics), so you need a negation for the TOP-LEVEL directory AND every intermediate directory in the path — otherwise chezmoi stops traversal at the first ignored entry and the file is never reached.

# GLOBAL PATTERNS
**/.DS_Store

# HOME DIRECTORY PATTERNS
# Sorted alphabetically, with directories grouped at the top.
